# SECOMM AI Toolkit — runtime only (Phase 1 carve-out, RM-02/RM-03)
# Generated per binding design SECOMM_AI_TOOLKIT_PHASE1_TARGET_DESIGN_DECISION.md §8.4 (Phase 1d).
# Scoped to .ai/ — does NOT modify the repo-root .gitignore.
# Durable project truth (.ai/project/, .ai/records/, .ai/workflow/ definitions, .ai/agents/, …) stays committable.

# Mutable runtime umbrella — session/, workflow/, evidence/, navigator workspace (RM-02/RM-03)
# Per-staff transient state is gitignored; skeleton dirs kept via .gitkeep so a fresh clone has
# the dirs present without depending on the agent to mkdir-on-write.
# NOTE: a tracked .gitkeep makes `git check-ignore .ai/runtime/` report "not ignored" (git quirk),
# so the toolkit validator's runtime-separation dir-check shows 1 cosmetic WARN. Contents ARE
# ignored — the WARN is a false positive; the toolkit validator should check a content file instead.
/runtime/**
!/runtime/**/
!/runtime/**/.gitkeep

# Legacy session-cursor files (Phase 1d RM-09: superseded, not deleted) → canonical home is .ai/runtime/session/
/project-context/memory/CURRENT_STATE.md
/project-context/memory/NEXT_TASK.md
/project-context/memory/RESEARCH_NOTES.md

# Initialization scratch
/initialization/draft.md
/initialization/CURRENT_INITIALIZATION_STATE.md

# Toolkit sync backups (transient — created by bin/project-ai-upgrade rollback safety)
/toolkit/_pre-sync-backup-*/
